Cipherframe invokes FFmpeg and FFprobe as separate processes and does not link
against them. FFmpeg is not distributed with the Cipherframe source code.

The worker container image (build/worker.Dockerfile) bundles FFmpeg and x264 as
separate programs next to the Cipherframe server. They are built from the pinned
upstream sources listed in the image and are licensed under the GNU General
Public License (version 2 or later; the FFmpeg binary is GPL because it is built
with x264). The image also contains dav1d (BSD-2-Clause) and the GNU C Library
(LGPL-2.1-or-later, linked statically). The licence texts and a written source
offer with the exact sources, checksums and build configuration are in the image
under /usr/share/licenses/ffmpeg/. Cipherframe's own code stays under the Apache
License 2.0. Operators who prefer not to distribute or run a GPL FFmpeg can use
their own FFmpeg through CIPHERFRAME_FFMPEG_PATH and CIPHERFRAME_FFPROBE_PATH.
H.264 patent licensing is the operator's responsibility.

YuNet face detection model (ml/Dockerfile)
------------------------------------------
The face masker image (ml/Dockerfile) bundles the YuNet face detection model
face_detection_yunet_2026may.onnx from the OpenCV Zoo
(https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo, models/face_detection_yunet), fetched at
a pinned commit and verified by SHA-256. It is licensed under the MIT License:

